WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:03.300
-Yet another MAGA Republican

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.467
handpicked by Donald Trump

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:06.434
has lost a key race
in a battleground state,

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:07.601
this time in Georgia,

00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:09.968
where Democratic incumbent
Raphael Warnock

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.434
won the Senate runoff
last night,

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:13.701
giving Democrats
full control of the chamber

00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:16.467
without needing a tiebreaker,
and defying the odds

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:19.067
in a year Republicans thought
would be a red wave.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:21.567
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:23.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.634
One way you know
that Herschel Walker

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:30.300
was deeply unqualified to serve
in the United States Senate

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.234
was that even Republicans
would rarely let him go

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:36.234
on Fox News by himself.

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:39.033
Instead, he was almost always
accompanied by a chaperone,

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:41.634
South Carolina Senator
Lindsey Graham,

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:43.667
who seemed to do
most of the talking.

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:46.167
-This is the year
of the Georgia Bulldog,

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:49.000
and there is no bigger Georgia
Bulldog than Herschel Walker.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.234
I want every liberal to be
miserable come election night.

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:53.701
TeamHerschel.com.

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:55.701
So, TeamHerschel.com,
if you want to close.

00:00:55.701 --> 00:00:57.601
-Yeah, go to TeamHerschel.com
and --

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:59.100
-But I want to say one thing.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.834
This man will change
the Republican Party.

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:03.467
You're gonna win this race.

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:05.801
TeamHerschel.com.

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:07.634
Go light up the internet.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.000
-Senator Graham, you --
-If you will give

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.334
to TeamHerschel.com
right now tonight,

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:15.834
I will do 50 push-ups
on your show.

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:17.334
but you got to give now.

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:21.234
-Man, I understand why they let
Lindsey Graham do the talking,

00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:24.167
but they didn't even trust
Herschel with the push-ups?

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:28.667
That's really a testament to how
little faith they had in him.

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.334
[As Graham] I'm not saying
Herschel's dumb,

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:32.901
but the last time I asked him
to give me 50 push-ups,

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:34.901
he robbed the bra store.

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:37.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:39.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:45.934
[Normal voice] But I have to
say, when I heard that,

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:47.334
I almost gave money
to Herschel Walker

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:48.834
because I would love
to see Lindsey Graham

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:50.133
attempt 50 push-ups.

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:52.567
[As Graham] Oh, I can do --
I can do 50 push-ups.

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:54.567
My meemaw made me do that
as a punishment

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:57.000
whenever I forgot to clean
her hemorrhoid donut.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.901
You can put it in the dishwasher
yourself, Meemaw!

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:02.901
I ain't cleanin' it anymore!

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:05.434
Fine!

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:08.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:11.434
One...

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:12.734
[Normal voice] By the way,
I'm not saying

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:13.901
I could bang out 50, either.

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:15.400
Here's how I do 50 push-ups.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.367
I do a set of 20, then 15,

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.634
ten, one, one, one,

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:20.834
one, one,

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:22.334
hospital.

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:23.667
Shockingly, the strategy

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:25.701
of doing exercise stunts
for money did not work.

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:28.300
Warnock beat Walker handily
last night in a state

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.534
where the Republican governor
won by eight points.

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:33.100
And one reason for that
is people are just tired

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:36.501
of Trump's handpicked clown car
of bozos and doofuses.

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:38.767
For example,
we told you a few weeks ago

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:41.434
about a very bizarre,
lengthy rant

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:43.701
Walker went on
at a campaign stop

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:46.033
about vampires and werewolves.

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:47.501
The story was so long
and detailed,

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:49.400
it would take us
the rest of this segment

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.400
to show you the whole thing,
but here's how it started.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.234
-You ever watch a stupid movie
late at night

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:54.667
hoping it gonna get better,
it don't get better,

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:56.300
but you keep watching it anyway?

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.467
'Cause the other night --

00:02:57.467 --> 00:02:59.200
the other night
I was watching this movie,

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.067
I was watching this movie
called "Fright Night,"

00:03:01.067 --> 00:03:02.767
"Freak Night" --
some type of night.

00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:04.834
But it was about vampires.
I don't know if you know --

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:06.868
vampires some cool people,
are they not?

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:08.868
But I'mma tell you something
that I found out.

00:03:08.868 --> 00:03:10.234
A werewolf can kill a vampire.

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:12.067
Did you know that?
I never knew that.

00:03:12.067 --> 00:03:13.434
So I don't want to be
a vampire anymore.

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:14.901
I want to be a werewolf.

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:17.334
-Herschel Walker wanted to be
a werewolf, but in reality,

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:20.367
he was really more of
a who-what-when-why-where-wolf.

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:21.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.801
In that every time that
he opened his mouth, you said,

00:03:23.801 --> 00:03:26.300
"What? When? Who? Why? Where?"

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.801
There was at least one
small victory

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:29.033
for Walker last night, though.

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:31.868
They asked the same question
in the exit polls,

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:35.334
and it turns out that vampires
are, in fact, cool people.

00:03:35.334 --> 00:03:37.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:39.000
Now, the reason
why we showed you that

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.834
is it actually played
a pretty big role

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:42.567
at the end of the runoff
when President Obama

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:44.234
went to Georgia
to campaign for Warnock

00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:45.901
and mocked Walker
for the vampire story.

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:47.400
In fact, Obama couldn't even

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.467
start talking about it
without laughing.

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.133
-Since the last time
I was here --

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:52.834
[ Laughing ]

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:54.434
Since the last time I was here,

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:58.067
Mr. Walker
has been talking about issues

00:03:58.067 --> 00:04:01.968
that are of great importance
to the people of Georgia,

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:05.300
like whether it's better
to be a vampire or a werewolf.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.601 --> 00:04:17.501
This is a debate that I must
confess I once had myself.

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:20.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.300
When I was seven.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:24.801 --> 00:04:26.634
Then I grew up.

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:28.601
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.434
In case you're wondering,
by the way,

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:36.567
Mr. Walker decided
he wanted to be a werewolf.

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:38.234
Which is great.

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:39.868
As far as I'm concerned,

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:42.267
he can be anything
he wants to be,

00:04:42.267 --> 00:04:44.834
except for
a United States senator.

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:45.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:48.133
-And I do...

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:50.801
I will say,

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:54.267
I do wish I could have seen
seven-year-old Obama debating

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:56.834
whether he wanted to be
a werewolf or a vampire.

00:04:56.834 --> 00:04:58.434
[As Obama] Uh, now,
on the one hand,

00:04:58.434 --> 00:05:01.667
vampires, they're immortal.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.834
On the other hand,

00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:05.834
werewolves can dunk.

00:05:05.834 --> 00:05:07.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.734 --> 00:05:10.901
[Normal voice]
Also, I want to say,

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:13.367
it is not fair
that in addition to being

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:14.801
one of the most skilled
politicians

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:16.467
and greatest orators
in American history,

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:19.467
Obama also has legit
comedy chops.

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:22.267
Like, it doesn't work
the other way.

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:24.834
None of my comedy friends
could ever be president.

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:29.234
Because first of all,
you got to get up before 11:00.

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:33.234
I'm pretty sure
they drug test you.

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:35.501
If a White House aide ever
has to utter the words,

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:40.033
"President Samberg,
the nukes are headed our way,"

00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:42.033
we're [bleep]

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:45.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.467
Mostly because --

00:05:47.467 --> 00:05:48.868
Mostly because if that happened,

00:05:48.868 --> 00:05:51.300
he would not stop doing
his Nicolas Cage impression.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.767
"Sir, we need to call

00:05:52.767 --> 00:05:54.634
the president of Russia
immediately."

00:05:54.634 --> 00:05:57.901
"Or I could break
into the Kremlin."

00:05:57.901 --> 00:05:59.701
"We do not have time
for your impressions, sir.

00:05:59.701 --> 00:06:01.434
They have already fired
their nukes."

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:03.767
"I just hope
they don't aim one

00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:05.601
at my doink!"

00:06:05.601 --> 00:06:07.434
[ Explosion ]

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:11.501
Walker was so deeply unqualified
that much of the time it seemed

00:06:11.501 --> 00:06:13.234
like he didn't even know
what was going on.

00:06:13.234 --> 00:06:15.467
Even Walker's fellow Republicans
warned months ago

00:06:15.467 --> 00:06:16.834
that he could lose.
The only reason

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:19.434
he was even a candidate
for Senate in the first place

00:06:19.434 --> 00:06:21.834
was that he was once
on Donald Trump's game show.

00:06:21.834 --> 00:06:23.834
Donald Trump fired him
from "The Celebrity Apprentice,"

00:06:23.834 --> 00:06:28.167
but thought he might do better
in the United States Senate.

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:29.834
[As Trump] Herschel,
I don't know if you're ready

00:06:29.834 --> 00:06:32.834
to sell corndogs
in Times Square.

00:06:32.834 --> 00:06:36.467
So let's put you in charge
of the US military first.

00:06:36.467 --> 00:06:38.133
[ Laughter ]

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:40.734
Besides, if you wanted to
nominate a game show contestant,

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:42.133
you could do much better.

00:06:42.133 --> 00:06:45.200
Just pick literally anyone who's
ever been on "Family Feud."

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:46.901
Well, anyone but this woman.

00:06:46.901 --> 00:06:50.133
-Name something that might be
all over a woman.

00:06:50.133 --> 00:06:51.400
Ale?

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:53.901
-I don't know how to say
this elegantly, but [bleep]

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.067
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:06:56.067 --> 00:06:58.634
-Good answer! Good answer!

00:06:58.634 --> 00:07:01.300
-We didn't bleep that.
They did.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.467
What did she say?!

00:07:03.467 --> 00:07:04.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.968 --> 00:07:08.901
What could the answer
have possibly been?

00:07:08.901 --> 00:07:11.834
Look what this woman did
to poor Steve Harvey.

00:07:11.834 --> 00:07:14.167
Do you know how filthy
your answer has to be

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:17.000
to completely silence
Steve Harvey?!

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:18.834
I've never seen
so much existential dread

00:07:18.834 --> 00:07:20.834
in one man's eyes.

00:07:20.834 --> 00:07:22.334
You know what
the worst part was?

00:07:22.334 --> 00:07:23.834
Number one answer.

00:07:23.834 --> 00:07:26.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:33.033
The point is, Walker is yet
another Trump-picked candidate

00:07:33.033 --> 00:07:34.367
who cost Republicans a seat

00:07:34.367 --> 00:07:35.701
that they had
very much hoped to win.

00:07:35.701 --> 00:07:37.033
Republicans were completely
on board

00:07:37.033 --> 00:07:38.534
and did everything they could
to help Walker win,

00:07:38.534 --> 00:07:40.968
despite the fact that he was
very obviously unqualified.

00:07:40.968 --> 00:07:42.334
But now,

00:07:42.334 --> 00:07:44.167
even many of Trump's former
allies are turning on him.

00:07:44.167 --> 00:07:45.734
Yesterday,
before the results even came in,

00:07:45.734 --> 00:07:49.033
Fox Business host Stuart Varney
laid into Trump

00:07:49.033 --> 00:07:51.367
for backing so many
losing candidates.

00:07:51.367 --> 00:07:53.033
-There's a lot at stake here.

00:07:53.033 --> 00:07:55.701
It's more than just the balance
of power in the Senate.

00:07:55.701 --> 00:07:58.033
It's about the state
of the Republican Party

00:07:58.033 --> 00:08:00.067
and Trump's role in it.

00:08:00.067 --> 00:08:04.400
He seems to be losing what used
to be his iron grip on the GOP.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.501
He still has a hard core
of supporters

00:08:06.501 --> 00:08:07.901
who will follow him regardless.

00:08:07.901 --> 00:08:12.434
But many of the 74 million
people who voted for him in 2020

00:08:12.434 --> 00:08:13.934
have been turned off.

00:08:13.934 --> 00:08:15.534
-It's such an indictment
of the GOP

00:08:15.534 --> 00:08:18.567
that Trump ever had an iron grip
on them to begin with.

00:08:18.567 --> 00:08:21.067
It's hard to imagine him
having an iron grip at all.

00:08:21.067 --> 00:08:23.567
I imagine shaking Trump's hand
feels a lot like

00:08:23.567 --> 00:08:26.400
holding a wet baby bird.

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:27.934
Say what you will
about the Democrats,

00:08:27.934 --> 00:08:29.767
I've never heard them refer
to any president,

00:08:29.767 --> 00:08:32.434
no matter how popular, as having
an iron grip on the party.

00:08:32.434 --> 00:08:33.734
No one talks like that

00:08:33.734 --> 00:08:35.234
unless they're in
"House of the Dragon."

00:08:35.234 --> 00:08:37.701
Although I do think
Trump could recapture

00:08:37.701 --> 00:08:39.033
some of that energy he once had

00:08:39.033 --> 00:08:40.601
if he just started
showing up to rallies

00:08:40.601 --> 00:08:43.634
wearing that golden mask
Viserys wears.

00:08:43.634 --> 00:08:44.801
[As Trump] Rhaenyra --

00:08:44.801 --> 00:08:46.300
We love Rhaenyra,
don't we, folks?

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:48.934
And don't forget about
her dragon Syrax.

00:08:48.934 --> 00:08:50.434
Syrax -- I met him once.

00:08:50.434 --> 00:08:51.834
Big dragon, tough dragon.

00:08:51.834 --> 00:08:53.334
He came up to me --

00:08:53.334 --> 00:08:55.534
He came up to me,
tears pouring down his face

00:08:55.534 --> 00:08:59.200
and then sizzling
in his fiery maw.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.834
And he clutched my entire body
in his giant talons

00:09:01.834 --> 00:09:04.834
and then he said to me,
he said, "Mr. Trump, sir? Roar!"

00:09:04.834 --> 00:09:08.167
And he breathed fire
all over me.

00:09:08.167 --> 00:09:11.334
But my skin is so thick
and resistant...

00:09:11.334 --> 00:09:13.000
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.667 --> 00:09:16.000
[ Laughter continues ]

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:17.934
...all it did was make me
look like this.

00:09:17.934 --> 00:09:20.601
So, there you go.

00:09:20.601 --> 00:09:22.868
[Normal voice] And Varney --
Varney wasn't the only one

00:09:22.868 --> 00:09:23.968
throwing shade at Trump

00:09:23.968 --> 00:09:25.801
after Warnock
was declared the winner.

00:09:25.801 --> 00:09:27.100
Fox host Laura Ingraham

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:29.334
and former Trump White House
aide Kellyanne Conway

00:09:29.334 --> 00:09:31.100
complained that,
for some reason,

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:32.767
Republicans weren't as good

00:09:32.767 --> 00:09:34.901
at using mail-in voting
as Democrats.

00:09:34.901 --> 00:09:38.167
-We need to not just compete
for votes, for ballots.

00:09:38.167 --> 00:09:39.667
We need to compete for ballots.

00:09:39.667 --> 00:09:42.000
If we don't bank ballots early,
we're going to keep losing.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.601
-But we didn't.
-But we didn't.

00:09:43.601 --> 00:09:45.067
-But we didn't do it in 2020

00:09:45.067 --> 00:09:47.067
'cause everyone said don't vote
early 'cause that's corrupt.

00:09:47.067 --> 00:09:50.067
-Not everyone.
-Well, a lot of people did.

00:09:50.067 --> 00:09:51.400
The very top of
the Republican Party.

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:52.567
You didn't.
-Yes, big-name people did.

00:09:52.567 --> 00:09:54.367
-Oh, did a lot of people

00:09:54.367 --> 00:09:56.167
at the very top
of the Republican Party

00:09:56.167 --> 00:09:57.501
say mail-in voting was corrupt?

00:09:57.501 --> 00:10:00.234
Huh! I wonder who
those people were.

00:10:00.234 --> 00:10:02.200
Even when they're obviously
talking about Trump,

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.701
they can't bring themselves
to say his name.

00:10:03.701 --> 00:10:05.234
From now on,
whenever someone says

00:10:05.234 --> 00:10:07.701
Trump's name on Fox News,
it's gonna sound like this.

00:10:07.701 --> 00:10:08.801
[Bleep]

00:10:08.801 --> 00:10:10.267
It's so amazing
to watch these people

00:10:10.267 --> 00:10:11.434
suddenly start complaining about

00:10:11.434 --> 00:10:13.100
the consequences
of their own actions.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:14.601
You were Trump's
fiercest supporters

00:10:14.601 --> 00:10:16.868
when he was claiming
mail-in voting led to fraud,

00:10:16.868 --> 00:10:19.133
and now you're whining that
Republicans don't vote by mail.

00:10:19.133 --> 00:10:22.133
Sorry, but you can't complain
about a neck bite

00:10:22.133 --> 00:10:24.033
after you open the door
and invite in a...

00:10:24.033 --> 00:10:25.033
-Vampire.

00:10:25.033 --> 00:10:27.100
-The best part...
[ Laughter ]

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.601
The best part, though,
was watching them melt down

00:10:29.601 --> 00:10:31.701
as the results came in
and desperately search

00:10:31.701 --> 00:10:34.200
for anyone
other than Trump to blame.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.634
-This is what we expected,
and now look.

00:10:36.634 --> 00:10:39.234
The Senate Democrats,
I would argue,

00:10:39.234 --> 00:10:42.534
did a much better job
and they got the early vote out.

00:10:42.534 --> 00:10:44.634
We felt this coming.

00:10:44.634 --> 00:10:48.801
To me, it never felt like
the Senate Republicans

00:10:48.801 --> 00:10:52.133
wanted this guy in office.

00:10:52.133 --> 00:10:54.767
He was a Trump pick.
They didn't like that.

00:10:54.767 --> 00:10:57.534
There wasn't the intensity
on the part of the Republicans

00:10:57.534 --> 00:10:59.434
as there was on the part
of the Democrats.

00:10:59.434 --> 00:11:01.167
I felt it. You felt it.

00:11:01.167 --> 00:11:02.834
But we don't change anything.

00:11:02.834 --> 00:11:04.934
We have the same people
in place in leadership.

00:11:04.934 --> 00:11:06.701
Same people in place,
apparently, at the RNC.

00:11:06.701 --> 00:11:08.667
That's not -- perhaps
that's not changing.

00:11:08.667 --> 00:11:10.467
We just keep doing the same
thing over and over again.

00:11:10.467 --> 00:11:12.167
I'm pissed tonight, frankly.

00:11:12.167 --> 00:11:14.534
-Alright, first of all,
Laura Ingraham has the energy

00:11:14.534 --> 00:11:16.701
of a country club patron
who's been made aware

00:11:16.701 --> 00:11:18.534
they've changed chefs.

00:11:18.534 --> 00:11:21.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:23.634
"They fired Mario?

00:11:23.634 --> 00:11:25.534
They fired my Mario?

00:11:25.534 --> 00:11:28.601
But he used to make the most
delightful chèvre brioche.

00:11:28.601 --> 00:11:31.601
I'm pissed."

00:11:31.601 --> 00:11:33.667
Second, you're mad
that Senate Republicans

00:11:33.667 --> 00:11:35.400
didn't want Walker to join them?

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:38.968
You think they wanted to spend
all their downtime between votes

00:11:38.968 --> 00:11:41.334
talking about whether vampires
are cooler than werewolves?

00:11:41.334 --> 00:11:43.601
You think that's
Mitch McConnell's idea

00:11:43.601 --> 00:11:45.100
of a good time?

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:47.033
Besides, you know
he's gonna pick vampires.

00:11:47.033 --> 00:11:50.033
He'd never side against
one of his own.

00:11:50.033 --> 00:11:53.300
I do enjoy imagining
that conversation, though.

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:54.968
[As McConnell]
Uh, Herschel, just remember,

00:11:54.968 --> 00:11:58.968
we, uh, need you to vote,
uh, no on the bill.

00:11:58.968 --> 00:12:00.367
Mm-hmm.

00:12:00.367 --> 00:12:02.567
Yeah, uh, Herschel,
we've been over this.

00:12:02.567 --> 00:12:06.300
Uh, vampires are cooler
than werewolves.

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:08.234
[ Laughter ]

00:12:08.234 --> 00:12:10.501
Uh-huh. Yeah, yeah. Mm.

00:12:10.501 --> 00:12:15.834
No, no, I know a werewolf
can kill a vampire, Herschel.

00:12:15.834 --> 00:12:17.267
Yeah, yeah. But, uh...

00:12:17.267 --> 00:12:18.934
But a vampire, Herschel...

00:12:18.934 --> 00:12:23.501
[ Laughter ]

00:12:23.501 --> 00:12:26.167
Yeah, but a vampire
can turn into a bat.

00:12:26.167 --> 00:12:27.868
[ Laughter ]

00:12:29.834 --> 00:12:31.000
He dropped the phone.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.667
[ Laughs ]

00:12:32.667 --> 00:12:34.601
[Normal voice]
Republicans are finally facing

00:12:34.601 --> 00:12:36.200
the political consequences
of their actions.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:38.067
Their unflinching loyalty
to Donald Trump

00:12:38.067 --> 00:12:39.234
is now destroying their party,

00:12:39.234 --> 00:12:40.734
and Walker is just
the latest example.

00:12:40.734 --> 00:12:43.000
He was deeply unqualified
to be a senator.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:45.667
On top of that, I'm not even
sure he wanted to be one.

00:12:45.667 --> 00:12:47.167
If only Republicans
had asked him

00:12:47.167 --> 00:12:48.968
what he actually wanted to be,
he could have told them...

00:12:48.968 --> 00:12:50.133
-I want to be a werewolf.

00:12:50.133 --> 00:12:52.300
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:55.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

